<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<title>Natan Admassu Portfolio</title>

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>

<style>
body {
    background-color: #f4f4f4;
    font-family: Arial;
    text-align: center;
    margin: 20px;
}

h1 {
    color: darkgreen;
}

.section {
    background-color: white;
    padding: 20px;
    margin: 20px auto;
    max-width: 800px;
}

img {
    width: 300px;
    max-width: 90%;
    margin: 10px;
}

canvas {
    max-width: 700px;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<h1>Natan Admassu</h1>
<h2>My Soccer Portfolio</h2>

<div class="section">
<h2>About Me</h2>
<p>My name is Natan Admassu. I am a Division I soccer goalkeeper at Binghamton University. Soccer has been a big part of my life, and I enjoy learning about sports and statistics.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>Soccer Photos</h2>

<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574629810360-7efbbe195018" alt="Soccer field">

<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1431324155629-1a6deb1dec8d" alt="Soccer players">
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>Chart 1: Saves Per Game</h2>
<p>This line graph shows example goalkeeper saves over five games.</p>
<canvas id="myChart"></canvas>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>Chart 2: Goals Allowed</h2>
<p>This bar graph shows example goals allowed over five games.</p>
<canvas id="myBarChart"></canvas>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>My Design Choices</h2>
<p>I decided to make my portfolio about soccer because it is something I enjoy and have been involved in for many years. I chose green for the title because it reminds me of a soccer field. I also used a light background with white sections to make everything easy to read. I included two soccer photos to match the theme of my website. For my charts, I used a line graph to show saves per game and a bar graph to show goals allowed. Overall, I wanted my website to look simple, clean, and organized.</p>
</div>

<script>

// Line Graph
const labels = ['Game 1', 'Game 2', 'Game 3', 'Game 4', 'Game 5'];

const data = {
    labels,
    datasets: [{
        label: 'Saves',
        data: [4, 6, 3, 7, 5],
        borderColor: 'green',
        borderWidth: 2,
        tension: 0.3
    }]
};

new Chart(document.getElementById('myChart'), {
    type: 'line',
    data,
    options: {
        scales: {
            y: {
                beginAtZero: true
            }
        }
    }
});

// Bar Graph
const barData = {
    labels,
    datasets: [{
        label: 'Goals Allowed',
        data: [2, 1, 0, 2, 1],
        backgroundColor: 'darkgreen'
    }]
};

new Chart(document.getElementById('myBarChart'), {
    type: 'bar',
    data: barData,
    options: {
        scales: {
            y: {
                beginAtZero: true
            }
        }
    }
});

</script>

</body>
</html>
